@prefix brick: <https://brickschema.org/schema/Brick#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# A small, acyclic excerpt of the real Brick class hierarchy (two branches,
# several hops deep, so the subClassOf+ property path actually has more
# than one step to traverse). No class is ever its own ancestor here --
# this fixture documents the steady state the real test protects: Brick.ttl
# is expected to have zero cycles, and that is the only branch reachable
# through run_pair (see meta.json / driver.py for why).
brick:Equipment rdfs:subClassOf brick:Entity .
brick:HVAC_Equipment rdfs:subClassOf brick:Equipment .
brick:Air_Handling_Unit rdfs:subClassOf brick:HVAC_Equipment .
# Redundant transitive edge (AHU is already a subClassOf Equipment through
# HVAC_Equipment): still acyclic, but it means "does any edge run directly
# between two nodes that are indirectly related anyway" is no longer
# vacuously false, so a query that gets the direction of the two
# interpolated terms wrong has something real to (wrongly) match.
brick:Air_Handling_Unit rdfs:subClassOf brick:Equipment .
brick:Point rdfs:subClassOf brick:Entity .
brick:Sensor rdfs:subClassOf brick:Point .
brick:Temperature_Sensor rdfs:subClassOf brick:Sensor .
brick:Zone_Air_Temperature_Sensor rdfs:subClassOf brick:Temperature_Sensor .
